<title>USA: Tropical storm threat to ships in western Pacific.</title>
<headline>Tropical storm threat to ships in western Pacific.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Storm Jimmy was a threat to shipping in the western Pacific, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp said on Friday.</p>
<p>Jimmy, with 55 mph winds near latitude 21n lontitude 156e, was moving north northeast at seven mph.</p>
<p>It was expected to turn back to the northeast, weaken, and dissipate in about 48 hours.</p>
